OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F344A1785331108
OL,3,CMan fined over #140 for stealing
OL,4,CGreggs snacks
OL,6,FProsecuting, Ms Begum told Birmingham
OL,7,FMagistrates' Court: "Staff became
OL,8,Fsuspicious and issued a warning that
OL,9,Fshoplifters would not be tolerated."
OL,11,FBrennan pleaded guilty to theft and
OL,12,Fwas fined #40, plus #85 prosecution
OL,13,Fcosts and a #16 victim surcharge. The
OL,14,Fgoods were recovered.
OL,16,FThe defendant had 21 previous
OL,17,Fconvictions for 40 offences, with his
OL,18,Fdefence lawyer saying there was
OL,19,F"little to no planning involved in
OL,20,Ftaking the items."
